{"kind":"propose","text":"ARC-1 proposes copying one admitted entry's retained inputs across bounded archive passes. Keep the existing attempt and input-work ceilings for each pass. Retain verified progress against the exact source scope and entry hash so a retry can resume the same input set. Confirmation and floor eligibility remain at the prior position until the complete entry and all required retained inputs are independently confirmed. A moved entry or unverified partial result must produce no forward progress. The observed 128-use fixture stopped on input work below the attempt cap, so changing only the attempt ceiling would leave the measured stop. A later implementation needs a real native control showing the largest admitted shape settles after multiple bounded passes, a restart resumes existing progress without accepting an incomplete receipt, and the floor waits until confirmation. The measured floor was disabled, so this last witness remains required. Please rule on the staged-copy rule before production source.","body":{"to":"planner"}}